2026-08-24T18:44:33Z	tried	what=the long-haul harness itself	config=tmhaul: repo-as-state-of-record, detached supervisor, cron heartbeat, 8 alarms, work-counting budget; tmresim as the first worker	produced=86 + 12 tests green; every alarm fired from a fixture and against a live process; a full bank does commit + paste mirror + GitHub push in about 70 s	claim=MEASURED	control=alarms selftest pairs each alarm with a state that must fire it AND a healthy control that must fire nothing; live-test runs four real workers (normal, stall, crash, silent) and reads the firings back off disk	why=Every failure the project hit on 2026-08-24 was a durability failure, not an algorithm failure. The five were: a supervising agent settling while its child ran; a stall detector that could not fire at zero evals; the 18-hour lease cap; a 30-day store used as a months-long one; and a budget clock burning during a stall. Each is answered by a mechanism rather than a note in a document, because a note does not fire at 3am.	node=117796
2026-08-24T18:44:33Z	tried	what=the standing re-simulation sweep as the harness's first real workload	config=tmresim --loop --pause-s 300, plain oracle in process via ghost::oracle::validate_many, batched one server launch per map	produced=7 of 7 tapes on Kacky Reloaded #290 re-simulated at exactly their published times in 6 s; the full sweep is 174 tapes across 36 maps	claim=MEASURED	control=the no-ghost gate is two-sided and tested: a human recording is refused, one of our own tapes is accepted, and a file nothing places is refused rather than assumed ours	why=The project's rule is that a banked result is re-simulated by the plain oracle standing, not as a spot check — and until now nothing made that true. It is also the right first job for the harness: hours long, countable, real failure modes, and it reads a corpus that is NOT in the repo, which is what surfaced the one real gap in the recovery story.	node=117796
